# Walkthrough — Brownfield Refactor: EF Core Persistence & Analytics Pipeline

## Summary

Introduced durable SQLite persistence via EF Core and a decoupled, bounded-channel analytics pipeline to the URL Shortener. All existing API contracts, response shapes, and unit tests are preserved.

---

## Changes Made

### Core Layer (2 new files)
| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| [`ClickEvent.cs`](file:///c:/Repos/URL-Shortener/src/UrlShortener.Core/Entities/ClickEvent.cs) | Analytics domain entity: Id, ShortCode, TimestampUtc, UserAgent, Referer |
| [`IAnalyticsService.cs`](file:///c:/Repos/URL-Shortener/src/UrlShortener.Core/Interfaces/IAnalyticsService.cs) | Non-blocking `void TrackClick(...)` interface — synchronous because it only does `TryWrite` |

### Infrastructure Layer — Persistence (3 files: 1 modified, 2 new)
| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
